course: dictionary
lesson: 5424
title: Ladybug: a small beetle with a big job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ladybug is a small round beetle, usually red or orange with black spots. In «Ladybirds, called ladybugs in North America, eat greenfly (aphids) that damage plants», the word «called» is a clue that ladybugs is another name for the same insect.
explain: The brackets are a clue too. «(aphids)» tells you that greenfly is another word for aphids, so you already know what the greenfly are: tiny insects that harm plants.
explain: Read on to find out why gardeners are glad to see them. The sentence says ladybugs eat the greenfly that damage plants, so you can work out that a ladybug is a helper in a garden. Try swapping your meaning in: "Gardeners are glad to see helpers that eat pests" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
fact: A ladybug is a small round beetle, usually red or orange with black spots.
fact: Ladybugs eat tiny insects called aphids.
fact: Ladybug is the American name; in Britain the same insect is often called a ladybird.
fact: Ladybugs go through four stages: egg, larva, pupa and adult.
fact: Their bright colours warn birds that they taste bad.
exercise: «Ladybirds, called ladybugs in North America, eat greenfly (aphids) that damage plants.» What is a ladybug? | A type of plant that grows in gardens | A kind of worm that lives in soil | A large grey bird that sings at dawn | *A small round beetle, usually red or orange with black spots
exercise: What do ladybugs eat? | Fish from rivers | *Tiny insects called aphids | Seeds from the ground | Leaves from the trees
exercise: Which word is the name for this insect used in North America? | ladybird | beetle | aphid | *ladybug
test: Why are gardeners glad to see ladybugs? | Because they make honey | Because they sting people | *Because they eat aphids that damage plants | Because they live in water
test: Why might a ladybug's bright colours be useful? | They are pretty for the flowers | They make it fly faster | *They warn birds that ladybugs taste bad | They help it hide from the sun
exam: Which stage comes straight after the egg in a ladybug's life cycle? | Pupa | Aphid | *Larva | Adult
